# Building differentiated apps for Android XR with 3D content

## Android XR
you can have headsets or glasses, they have two modes

* Home Space: You have several apps oppened


* Full Space: You can only have one app open and it will provide a "bubble" view. Here you use the "SceneCore API" in the Jetpack XR SDK to take advantage of the spatial capabilities of Android XR. Here we have `SkyBox` and `Geometry`, you can think of Skybox as a distant image like a photosphere that surrounds you, it creates the illusion of a distant background. `Geometry` on the other hand, adds shape and depth, this creates a parallax effect, usually used to show the ground and objects near the user

    In full space you have the option to display videos in 180 or 360 degrees 

