# Mastering text input in Compose

## State-bases Textfields
Is a new best practice for TextField usage in compose. With this google has switched to a new state hoisting paradigm, by replacing value and callback hoisting the TextField state provides a more complete and reliable approach to managing the state of a Textfield, the `onValueChange" call back has been replaced with the new `InputTransformation` mechanism for handling input modifications. `VisualTransformation` has been updated to `OutputTransformation` for managing how text is presented. Single and multi line configurations are tidied up

Now you can enable Autofill in your textfields you just need to add a modifier called `semantics` and then specify it's `contentType`

## New `SecureTextField` and `OutlinedSecureTextField`
* Hides password by default
* Disable cut and copy actions

## textObfuscationMode
Allows you to define the visibility of the text in a `SecureTextField`. You have three options

* Visible: Shows anything you type
* Hidden: hides all character input
* RevealLastTyped: shows the last character typed for a set ammount of time

## Customize a TextField(`BasicTextField`)
`BasicTextField` is the base of all TextFields, You can create an OTP view to enter an OTP password by customizing the `decorator` parameter you can watch this video to get the code snippets

## `contentReceiver` Modifier
Experimental Foundation(added in version 1.7.0) API, it works with the new TextFields. Adding this modifier to a TextField is enough to let the keyboard know this TextField now supports GIFs, stickers and any other rich content, but this modifier takes a lambda that receives a `transferableContent` object, this object is basically a wrapper around clip data and clip description APIs, you can learn more about how to handle this type of data [here](goo.gle/rich-content). You can apply this modifier to any composable

## `autoSize` Parameter
New textFields and BasicText have a new parameter called `autoSize`, this can help the text you enter to occupy as much space as possible

## Autoformatting
Bellow is the flow of how inpuit and output transformations happen

Software keyboard/Hardware Keyboard/Clipboard Paste/Selection > InputTransformation > TextFiedlState > OutputTransformation > TextField

You can think of `InputTransformation` as a filter function, and using it we can limit the length, for example when entering a USA phone number which is 10 digits you can limit the input length and also only allow numbers/digits to be passed in, you can customize the `inputTransformation` parameter with a code like the following

```
InputTransformation.maxLength(10).then {
    if(!TextUtilx.isDigitsOnly(asCharSequence())) {
        revertAllChanges()
    }
}
```

With this we have only 10 digits, but now we need to format the text and we can do this in the `outputTransformation` step, we will use `TextFieldBuffer`, is a buffer that can be edited and provides methods for changing text(similar to StringBuilder)

However you could use Regex to do all of this formatting

